{"headerTitle":"CSTAT (Mean Time to Resolution)","showHeaderSeparator":false,"description":"Definition: CSAT is a metric used to measure a customer's satisfaction with a specific, single interaction, product, or service.

Focus: It is transactional and short-term, capturing how a customer feels immediately following a specific touchpoint, such as the closing of a support ticket.
